--- encoding -- generic encoding to/from string forms for the handl runtime.
---
--- Contract surface for the `encoding` stdlib interface: 2 functions
--- covering encoding of a `serde_json::Value` to a string form (e.g. base64,
--- hex) and decoding of a value back into a `Value`. The `cap`/`op`/
--- `handle` decls below declare the capability and signature surface;
--- `plugin-lib-stdlib`'s `encoding` `ModuleSpec` loads this file via
--- `include_str!` and its `cap` lines feed the plugin capability surface.
---
--- The functions are pure `.hnl` field-calls on the codec record — there
--- is no native impl or registry (the old `EncodingRegistry` /
--- `plugin-lib-encoding` path is gone).
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- encoding.encode -- encode a value into a string form using a named codec.
--- encoding.decode -- decode a value into a value using a named codec.
cap "encoding.encode"
cap "encoding.decode"
op "encoding.encode" : (Value * Value) ~> String
  guarantee: True
op "encoding.decode" : (Value * Value) ~> Value
  guarantee: True
handle "encoding.encode" with encode
handle "encoding.decode" with decode

--- Codec dispatch: the codec object is a record carrying `encode`/`decode`
--- arrows — produced by `hex.codec`/`base64.codec`/… — so `encoding.*` is a
--- pure `.hnl` field-call; no Rust registry needed.
export encode := (v, codec_obj) ~> (codec_obj.encode)(v)
export decode := (v, codec_obj) ~> (codec_obj.decode)(v)
